#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""SYRD-419: the new project's launcher artifacts, against the launcher they came out of.

The six definitions that build a new project's launcher config and write it
with its layout template moved unchanged into `scripts/new_project_artifacts.py`,
and the launcher re-exports all six. This pins what makes that safe:

- **No cycle, one set of objects**, whichever module is imported first; the
  module alone loads only the `ticket_board` modules its default comes from;
  the definition-time defaults (the default implementer roles, `print`) are
  the objects the launcher bound; the plan type is imported under TYPE_CHECKING.
- **Seams (rule 24):** every name the six read -- each other, the visible-pane
  cap, the default role CLIs, the layout payload, the JSON reader and atomic
  writer, the session, worktree and `.switchyard` directories, the onboarding
  seed and file name, the shared pane launcher -- is read through the launcher
  as often as before, so a patch there reaches it: cases below rebind the cap
  and the directory name on the launcher and see the effect.
- **Callers:** `new_project_command` calls the writer by its launcher global;
  no production module outside the launcher reads any of the six.
- **The behaviour is the baseline's:** role order and deduplication, chosen
  CLIs, models and efforts (blank ones omitted), slots and detachment at the
  cap and its notice, every path and board field, upstream settings, the
  designer and director environments and seed, the workflow projection and
  re-layout, the desktop policy, the layout-then-config write order, the mode
  the config is left with, and every error. `GOLDEN` below was produced by
  running the BASELINE launcher's own functions over the very cases embedded
  here (`gold419.py`), not typed; it is byte-identical whether generated under
  `env -i` or in a normal role pane.

Every case writes into its own test-owned output directory; the account- and
host-dependent seams and the workflow projection stand in, recorded. Spawns,
every exec, signals, account and group lookups and socket connections are
refused for each case.
"""

